Q2. [sec_eavailw.tex EW15]
BEFORE: The event-loop output files also store truth hadronic diagnostics: the proton and pion multiplicities and the leading-hadron angle.
AFTER: The event-loop output files also store truth hadronic diagnostics: the proton and pion multiplicities and the polar angle of the summed momentum of all final-state particles other than muons and neutrinos.

Q3. [sec_eavailw.tex EW75]
BEFORE: \begin{figure}[H] \centering \includegraphics[width=0.99\textwidth]{eavailW_band} \caption{Unfolded $(\Eavail,W)$ cross section versus the four-generator band (GENIE~CV, GENIE$+$MEC, NuWro, GiBUU; GENIE and NuWro flux-corrected, \S\ref{sec:3d-models}). Every generator lies below the data in the high-$W$, high-$\Eavail$ corner --- GENIE and NuWro by about their overall normalization shortfall, GiBUU by more; adding 2p2h leaves the corner unchanged because 2p2h populates low $W$.} \label{fig:eavailWband} \end{figure} MINERvA shallow-inelastic neutrino and antineutrino measurements also report shape and normalization disagreements with generators \cite{MINERvA:2026sis}.
AFTER: \begin{figure}[H] \centering \includegraphics[width=0.99\textwidth]{eavailW_band} \caption{Projections of the unfolded $(\Eavail,W)$ cross section onto $\Eavail$ (left) and $W$ (right), with the predictions of four generators (GENIE~CV, GENIE$+$MEC, NuWro, GiBUU; GENIE and NuWro flux-corrected, \S\ref{sec:3d-models}). In the high-$W$, high-$\Eavail$ corner, which the projections do not resolve, every generator lies below the data (\S\ref{sec:eavailw-band}) --- GENIE and NuWro by about their overall normalization shortfall, GiBUU by more; adding 2p2h leaves the corner essentially unchanged because 2p2h populates low $W$.} \label{fig:eavailWband} \end{figure} MINERvA shallow-inelastic neutrino and antineutrino measurements also report shape and normalization disagreements with generators \cite{MINERvA:2026sis}.

